When a window’s associated document has no navigable yet, Ladybird’s
push/replace/reload navigate event skips informing the navigation API
about aborting navigation, then returns false for a document that
isn’t fully active. Gecko gets the same result: Its Navigation::
FirePushReplaceReloadNavigateEvent() calls the Navigation’s own
InnerInformAboutAbortingNavigation(), which aborts its ongoing navigate
events and never reaches a navigable, and then returns false. Blink’s
NavigationApi::DispatchNavigateEvent() returns kContinue when
HasEntriesAndEventsDisabled(), so there the reload goes ahead.
